# Ford Zephyr Mk II four-door saloon, 1956-1962.
#
# The six-cylinder member of the 1956 'Three Graces' range, with the longer
# bonnet, the wide grille and the small tail fins. 4.534 m on the 2.718 m
# wheelbase.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Zephyr
#
# Dimensions 4.534 x 1.702 m, wheelbase 2.718 m. Height was not established.
#
# Shape reference: NO true level side elevation exists. Image 1 is a front
# three-quarter about 35 degrees off square; the flank is estimated from it
# and the other views within the published dimensions. The limitation is
# recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (d) for a model-specific list, grade (c) only for the later
# 1959-62 corporate palette. Savoy Black, Ermine White, Ambassador Blue and
# Goodwood Green. Weights 20, 18, 17, 15, total 70, provisional.
#
# Speed 140 km/h. Comfort 58/417, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 58. Classes 2,3.
# Dates are road presence: 1956 intro, retires staggered 1978-1981.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/ford-zephyr-mk2.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/ford-zephyr-mk2.dae. References:
# citycars/references/ford-zephyr-mk2/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: there is no true side elevation, so the flank is
# estimated. The wraparound glass is too flat, and the front wing transitions and
# tail trim are simplified. The model height of 1.50 m is an estimate, no
# published height having been established. At 128 px the broad grille, small
# fins and three-box body read as a Zephyr Mk II.


obj=citycar
